(Title) Tj
T*
(Behaviour change intervention during cardiac rehabilitation did not enhance physical) Tj
T*
(activity adherence beyond standard programs at six-month follow-up) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Objectives: Cardiac rehabilitation programs successfully promote acute increases in) Tj
T*
(physical activity, but durability of these gains remains uncertain. We tested whether) Tj
T*
(augmenting standard rehabilitation with targeted behaviour-change sessions would sustain) Tj
T*
(higher activity levels. Methods: Ninety-six patients from six cardiac clinics were) Tj
T*
(cluster-randomized to receive either standard care \(usual rehabilitation schedule\) or) Tj
T*
(usual rehabilitation plus structured behaviour counselling \(6 sessions over 16 weeks\).) Tj
T*
(Primary outcome: accelerometer-derived moderate-to-vigorous activity minutes and daily) Tj
T*
(steps at 6 months. Results: At 6-month assessment, mean daily MVPA was 38 minutes in the) Tj
T*
(standard-care group versus 41 minutes in the behaviour-intervention group \(difference 3) Tj
T*
(minutes; 95% CI -5 to 11 minutes; p=0.31\). Daily steps were similar \(6,892 versus 7,134;) Tj
T*
(p=0.42\). No between-group differences were observed in self-rated health, quality of life,) Tj
T*
(or mental well-being. Conclusion: The behaviour intervention did not produce clinically) Tj
T*
(meaningful improvements beyond standard rehabilitation, possibly because both groups) Tj
T*
(maintained excellent activity levels through ongoing program participation.) Tj
